# The `|| true` calls are inside the `#DEBHELPER#` block that
# dh_installsystemd generates, not hand-written here, and they are deliberate: a
# unit that cannot be unmasked or enabled on a system not running systemd must
# not make the install fail. This is the standard shape for any package using
# dh_installsystemd.
maintainer-script-ignores-errors

# The project ships no man page, so this package has none. docs/CLI.md and
# docs/CONFIGURATION.md are installed under /usr/share/doc/ananicy-rs/ instead,
# flattened rather than under a docs/ subdirectory, which is what dh_installdeb
# does with `debian/ananicy-rs.docs`. README.Debian says where they are.
# Writing a man page inside the packaging would create a second copy of the
# command-line reference to keep in step with the binary; it belongs upstream,
# next to the code it documents, and that is a change to propose rather than one
# to smuggle in via a recipe.
no-manual-page

# Expected for a package that has never been uploaded: there is no bug to close
# on the initial upload. It goes away by itself once there is an upload behind
# this one.
initial-upload-closes-no-bugs
